e-Metric-Space-September-26-2026.html#thm:blocks","release_id":"openai-math","schema":"statement-map-web/2","section":1,"section_title":"Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f633a66c7b2eea0bbadad875900fb691e42c2d81865ad800cb2c4636fa6ee7a5","file":"preprints/Failure-of-Bounded-Approximation-in-a-Lipschitz-Free-Space-over-a-Uniformly-Discrete-Metric-Space-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":92,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e5157be2428cc1605d40306d8ce1c1743b7a779439f491ddab9bcd8613e56d64","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Failure-of-Bounded-Approximation-in-a-Lipschitz-Free-Space-over-a-Uniformly-Discrete-Metric-Space-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f633a66c7b2eea0bbadad875900fb691e42c2d81865ad800cb2c4636fa6ee7a5","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Failure-of-Bounded-Approximation-in-a-Lipschitz-Free-Space-over-a-Uniformly-Discrete-Metric-Space-September-26-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L92"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:blocks}\nFor each integer $p\\ge1$, there are a bounded countably infinite pointed\nmetric space $(M_p,d_p,o)$ and a finite set $A_p\\subseteq M_p$ containing\n$o$ such that\n\\[\n d_p(x,y)\\ge1\\quad(x\\ne y),\\qquad\n \\operatorname{diam}M_p\\le B_p:=300p^2+150p+5,\n\\]\nand every bounded finite-rank linear operator\n$T_0:\\F(M_p)\\to\\F(M_p)$ with $\\norm{T_0}\\le p$ satisfies\n\\[\n \\max_{a\\in A_p}\\norm{T_0\\delta_a-\\delta_a}\\ge\\frac12.\n\\]"}
